  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 602.03 Back dune",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 602.03 “Back dune” means the secondary complex of ridges or mounds of sand that form from continued wind-blown sand transport through breaches in the fore dune and across the dune slack area, typically developing adjacent to a bordering surface water or wetland.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
